    <h2 id="overview">1. Overview</h2>
    <p>This Cancellation &amp; Refund Policy explains how you can cancel a Tycoon Clap service and when you may be entitled to a refund. It applies to our Growth Marketing, Software Engineering, and Data &amp; AI services, as well as B2B lead lists purchased from our Leads page. It should be read together with our <a href="terms-of-service.html">Terms of Service</a>.</p>
    <p>Our aim is simple: if we haven't delivered what we agreed, we'll make it right. If you've received the work you paid for, we may keep the fees for that work. If your proposal or signed agreement contains different cancellation or refund terms, those terms apply to that engagement.</p>

    <h2 id="how-to-cancel">2. How to cancel</h2>
    <p>To cancel a service, email <a href="mailto:nathalie@tycoonclap.com">nathalie@tycoonclap.com</a> with the subject line <strong>"Cancellation Request"</strong> and include:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Your name, company, and the email used for the engagement or purchase</li>
      <li>The service or order you want to cancel (and the invoice or order number, if you have it)</li>
      <li>The date you want the cancellation to take effect</li>
      <li>Optionally, a short note on why — we use feedback to improve</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We will confirm receipt by email within 2 business days. Notice periods are counted from the date we receive your written request. Cancelling by phone, chat, or social media is not sufficient, but we will always point you to the right channel.</p>

    <h2 id="by-service">3. Cancellation terms by service</h2>
    <table class="data-table">
      <tr><th>Service</th><th>How to cancel</th><th>What happens to fees</th></tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Growth Marketing</strong><br>(monthly retainers)</td>
        <td>15 days' written notice. Work continues through the notice period.</td>
        <td>The current billing period is not refunded once work has started. Fees for the notice period remain payable. No refund for months already delivered.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Software Engineering</strong><br>(fixed-price projects)</td>
        <td>Written notice at any time. Work stops on receipt, or on a handover date we agree.</td>
        <td>You pay for milestones completed and work in progress up to the cancellation date. Unstarted milestones paid in advance are refunded, less any non-recoverable third-party costs.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Software Engineering</strong><br>(time &amp; materials)</td>
        <td>7 days' written notice.</td>
        <td>You pay for hours worked up to the end of the notice period. Unused prepaid hours are refunded.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Data &amp; AI</strong><br>(projects and retainers)</td>
        <td>Projects: written notice at any time. Retainers: 15 days' written notice.</td>
        <td>Projects follow the milestone approach above. Retainers follow the Growth Marketing approach above.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Strategy calls &amp; audits</strong></td>
        <td>Reschedule or cancel at least 24 hours before the scheduled time.</td>
        <td>Full refund for prepaid sessions cancelled in time. No refund for no-shows or sessions already delivered.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>B2B Lead Lists</strong></td>
        <td>Digital product — see <a href="#leads">Section 5</a>.</td>
        <td>Not refundable after delivery, except as described in Section 5.</td>
      </tr>
    </table>

    <h2 id="eligibility">4. When you are eligible for a refund</h2>
    <div class="split">
      <div class="panel ok">
        <h4>✓ Refunds we will make</h4>
        <ul>
          <li>You were charged more than once for the same invoice or order</li>
          <li>You paid in advance for work or a session that we did not start or deliver</li>
          <li>We cancelled the engagement and you prepaid for work not yet performed</li>
          <li>We materially failed to deliver the agreed scope after you gave us written notice and a reasonable chance (normally 10 business days) to fix it</li>
          <li>A lead-list file was never delivered, is corrupted, or is materially different from its description (see Section 5)</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="panel no">
        <h4>✕ Refunds we cannot make</h4>
        <ul>
          <li>Work already delivered and accepted, or fees for the period in which work was performed</li>
          <li>Change of mind, change of business plans, or budget changes after work has started</li>
          <li>Business results that did not meet expectations (for example fewer leads or lower ROAS), since outcomes are not guaranteed</li>
          <li>Delays or issues caused by missing access, content, or approvals from your side</li>
          <li>Issues caused by third-party platforms, such as ad-account suspensions or policy changes</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2 id="leads">5. B2B lead lists</h2>
    <p>Lead lists are digital products delivered electronically after payment, and the data is available to you immediately on delivery. For that reason:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>No refunds after delivery</strong> for change of mind, or for data you have already downloaded and used.</li>
      <li><strong>Non-delivery or corrupted file:</strong> if you did not receive your file, or it cannot be opened, tell us within 7 days of purchase. We will re-send it or, if we cannot, refund you in full.</li>
      <li><strong>Materially different from description:</strong> if the list is substantially different from what was described on the Leads page (for example the wrong industry, geography, or job titles), contact us within 7 days with details. We will replace it with a corrected list or issue a refund.</li>
      <li><strong>Data accuracy:</strong> business contact data naturally goes out of date. A normal rate of bounced emails or changed roles does not by itself qualify for a refund. We may, at our discretion, offer a partial replacement for clearly inaccurate records reported promptly.</li>
      <li><strong>Misuse:</strong> no refunds will be given where the list has been shared, resold, or used in breach of our Terms of Service.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="non-refundable">6. Non-refundable costs</h2>
    <p>The following are not refundable, as they are paid to or committed with third parties:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Advertising spend</strong> you paid directly to platforms such as Google or Meta. Please manage budgets and billing in your own ad account.</li>
      <li>Third-party licences, tools, domains, hosting, stock assets, and app-store fees purchased for your project.</li>
      <li>Payment-processor fees and bank or currency-conversion charges, where these cannot be recovered from the processor.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="process">7. How refunds are processed</h2>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li><strong>Send your request.</strong> Email <a href="mailto:nathalie@tycoonclap.com">nathalie@tycoonclap.com</a> with the subject "Refund Request," your order or invoice number, and the reason.</li>
      <li><strong>We review it.</strong> We will acknowledge your request within 2 business days and give you a decision within 5 business days. We may ask for details or supporting screenshots.</li>
      <li><strong>Decision and amount.</strong> If approved, we will tell you the refund amount, including any deductions for work already completed or non-recoverable costs.</li>
      <li><strong>Refund issued.</strong> We refund to your original payment method (PayPal, Stripe, or bank transfer). Most refunds reach you within 5–10 business days, depending on your bank or provider.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>Refunds are made in the original currency of payment. Exchange-rate differences between payment and refund are outside our control. Where a refund is for part of an order only, we will set out the calculation in our email.</p>

    <h2 id="our-cancellation">8. If we cancel or pause a service</h2>
    <p>We may cancel or pause a service if you breach our Terms, an invoice remains unpaid after notice, we cannot get the access or information we need to continue, or continuing would break the law or a platform's rules. If we cancel for reasons other than your breach, we will refund any prepaid fees for work not yet performed.</p>

    <h2 id="disputes">9. Chargebacks and disputes</h2>
    <p>Please contact us before raising a payment dispute or chargeback with your bank, card issuer, PayPal, or Stripe. Most issues can be resolved faster directly. If a chargeback is filed for a service that was delivered, we may provide evidence of the work and communications to the payment provider and may suspend further work until the matter is resolved.</p>

    <h2 id="taxes">10. Taxes and fees on refunds</h2>
    <p>Where tax was charged on an invoice, the tax portion of a refund will be adjusted in line with the refunded amount and applicable law. We may issue a credit note for refunded invoices.</p>

    <div class="legal-note">This policy is provided as a general template for a service business and is not a substitute for legal advice. Notice periods, timelines, and refund conditions should match what you actually offer, and may need to be reviewed by a qualified attorney for the jurisdictions you serve. Consumers in some regions have mandatory statutory rights that this policy does not limit.</div>

    <h2 id="changes">11. Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>We may update this policy from time to time. The "Last updated" date at the top shows the latest revision. The version in force when you placed your order or signed your proposal applies to that order or engagement.</p>

    <h2 id="contact">12. Contact us</h2>
    <p>For any questions about cancellations or refunds, or to submit a request, contact us at:</p>
    <p><a href="mailto:nathalie@tycoonclap.com">nathalie@tycoonclap.com</a></p>
